findings.body:
The new authentication paths are untested end to end:
- backup-code login in `authorize`;
- consumption of a used code, so reuse must fail;
- disabling 2FA with a backup code.

The PR only exercises the download and copy buttons and leaves a TODO. The existing assertion `expect(page.locator(...).isChecked()).toBeTruthy()` checks a Promise and is always truthy, as the added FIXME admits. These are security-relevant flows and should have coverage before merging.
